# Example crontab entries for GithubSlashboard (Linux, and macOS if you prefer
# cron to launchd).
#
# Install with:
#   crontab -e        # then paste the lines below
#   crontab -l        # verify
#
# Notes:
#   - Point cron at the wrapper script, not the binary, so the GitHub token is
#     fetched at run time rather than stored in your crontab. See
#     run-githubslashboard.sh in this directory.
#   - cron runs with a very small PATH and does not read your shell profile. The
#     wrapper sets PATH itself, which is the main reason to use it here.
#   - Times are the machine's local time.
#   - Redirect output somewhere you will actually look; cron mails it by default.

# Every hour from 06:00 to 17:00, Monday to Friday.
0 6-17 * * 1-5 /home/example/.local/bin/run-githubslashboard.sh >> /home/example/.local/state/githubslashboard.log 2>&1

# Alternative: three fixed times on weekdays.
# 0 6,12,17 * * 1-5 /home/example/.local/bin/run-githubslashboard.sh >> /home/example/.local/state/githubslashboard.log 2>&1

# Alternative: every 45 minutes during working hours on weekdays.
# */45 6-17 * * 1-5 /home/example/.local/bin/run-githubslashboard.sh >> /home/example/.local/state/githubslashboard.log 2>&1
